				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5713ad64 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="5713ad64" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					
<div class="gwd">
<section style="background:#FBFAFE">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center">
      <span class="kicker">Sharjah questions</span>
      <h2 style="margin-top:14px">What Sharjah owners ask us first</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details open><summary>Does my Sharjah clinic need SHA approval to run Instagram or Google ads?</summary><p>For medical advertising, yes. Sharjah Health Authority publishes a "medical advertisement licence" service for SHA-licensed facilities and practitioners. Its stated conditions include prior approval from MOHAP, submission of the actual ad files, and a fresh application whenever the ad changes; the listed processing time is 8 working days. We build that lead time into every clinic campaign plan.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is a Sharjah clinic regulated by MOHAP or by Sharjah Health Authority?</summary><p>Both play a part. Private clinics in Sharjah are licensed by SHA, which was set up in 2010 to regulate healthcare in the emirate. For advertising, SHA's own service requires MOHAP's prior approval before it issues its ad licence. Federal government facilities in Sharjah are outside SHA's 2025 regulation decision.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How do Sharjah's decency rules affect salon advertising?</summary><p>Sharjah's decency rules, in force since 2001, set expectations on dress and behaviour in public places, and they shape what local audiences see as appropriate. In practice we keep Sharjah creative modest: no revealing outfits, focus on the treatment result, and clear signals that a ladies salon is women-only and private. Meta and Google's own policies on personal health and body imagery still apply on top.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Most of my clients work in Dubai. How do we stop them booking there instead?</summary><p>Be the easiest option at home. That means appearing for searches made from their building in the evening, replying on WhatsApp within minutes (our booking bot covers late hours), showing clear prices and opening times on Google, and running ads when they're back in Sharjah, not while they're at the office.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What does Sharjah Municipality look at before a ladies salon can open?</summary><p>The municipality's Health Control Section inspects the premises, approves the décor plan and does a final inspection. Every worker needs an occupational health card from the municipality's Public Health Clinic and hepatitis B vaccination records, and the salon needs a valid trade licence and a pest-control contract. Check the current guide with the municipality before you commit to a fit-out.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>				</div>
